  "title": "Tag navigator \u00b7 Level 2: The printed order",
  "brief": "Visit the four stations in the order on line 1 of the program, the one statement order = [a, b, c, d] (tag ids): on a scored run the runner fills it in; practice runs without it, so practise with seed 0's: order = [3, 1, 2, 0]. Four 100 mm ArUco tags (DICT_4X4_50, ids 0-3), each on an orange post with its middle 150 mm up: tag 0 at (100, 900) facing +x, tag 1 at (1200, 1700) facing -y, tag 2 at (2300, 900) facing -x, tag 3 at (1200, 100) facing +y, on a 2.4 x 1.8 m walled field. Station k is 300 mm in front of tag k: (400, 900), (1200, 1400), (2000, 900), (1200, 400). A station is visited when the robot's centre (the axle's middle) stays within 100 mm of it, facing its tag within 15 degrees, moving slower than 5 mm/s and turning slower than 5 degrees a second, for the whole of 0.5 s. Run 1 starts at (1200, 900) facing +x; runs 2-10 start anywhere in the 500 mm box in the middle (x 950-1450, y 650-1150), at any heading. T is the time to the last station's visit (the end of its 0.5 s stop), in the order, which ends the run; 120 s if the four are not visited in the order. Per run: 100 x min(1, par / T) - 0.25 x the mean stop error (mm: the centre's distance from the station at each counted visit) - 25 per station not visited in the order (a visit counts only at the next station due), at least 0. Pass: a mean of at least 60 with 8 of 10 runs visiting all four in the order. Par 17.1 s. No course run sees a tag until LINK or BCAM gives it a camera.",
